3. REMEDIATION RECOMMENDATIONS
* Fix for BOLA:
  Implement object-level authorization checks server-side. Before returning any
  profile data, the server needs to confirm that the requesting user either owns
  that account or holds admin-level permissions — the ID in the URL should never
  be trusted on its own.

* Fix for Brute-Force on Discount Field:
  Add rate limiting and a cooldown mechanism to the checkout endpoint. After a
  set number of failed attempts, the server locks out that IP or account for a
  period of time. That alone makes a sequential brute-force attack completely
  impractical.